justin timberlake breaks his silence  with an apology to britney spears  after coming under fire for the way he  handled their split  in the early 2000s oh and while he's at  it  he's saying he's sorry to janet jackson  too the recent backlash stems from the  new york times presents framing britney  spears documentary that premiered  last week throughout the unauthorized  project footage shows  spears being put in the hot seat and  questioned about her role in her highly  publicized breakup with timberlake  he's gone on television and pretty much  said  you broke his heart you did something  that caused him so much pain  so much suffering what did you do  at the time timberlake was seemingly  glorified  and had this to say in a new york radio  interview when he was asked if he had  ever had sex with spears  who had previously publicly declared she  was saving herself for  marriage yes or no oh man come on man  okay i did it many viewers reacted on  social media after watching the doc  with several arguing that timberlake was  to blame for the media's negative  portrayal of the pop star  after their split while others brought  up his behavior towards janet jackson  after the infamous wardrobe malfunction  that occurred during their super bowl  halftime performance in 2004  in a statement posted to timberlake's  instagram on friday  the singer said that he's seen the  messages tags comments and concerns  and he is deeply sorry quote i  understand that i fell  short in these moments and in many  others and benefited from a system that  condones misogyny  and racism i specifically want to  apologize to britney spears and janet  jackson both  individually because i care for and  respect these women  and i know i failed justin added that he  doesn't want to ever benefit from others  being  pulled down again quote i want to take  accountability for my own missteps in  all of this as well as be a part of a  world that uplifts  and supports i care deeply about the  well-being of the people i love  and have loved i can do better and i  will do better  e.t has reached out to spears and  jackson for comment  as for the baby one more time singer a  source told e.t  earlier this week that she is aware of  the documentary but hasn't watched it  and e.t source added that spears has  no interest in getting involved with any  details being discussed about her past  relationship with justin timberlake  she wouldn't want her fans to speak  negatively about him because she has the  utmost respect for both justin  and his wife jessica beale
 

